coder › Changed `toCsv` in `src/csv.ts` to prevent CSV formula injection, on branch `fix/csv-formula-injection`:

- `field()` now branches on `typeof cell === 'number'` and writes it plainly via `String(cell)`, so `-5` stays `-5`.
- A `string` field whose first char matches `/^[=+\-@\t\r]/` is written as `"'<text>"` (single quote prefixed, whole field double-quoted), with `"` inside doubled to `""`, e.g. `=HYPERLINK("http://x")` → `"'=HYPERLINK(""http://x"")"`.
- All other strings keep the existing rule: quote only if containing `,`, `"`, or `\n`, doubling inner `"`.

Commits:
- `83e0ab8` Escape formula-like string fields in toCsv
- `06b4859` Add tests for CSV formula escaping

Tests added in `src/csv.test.ts`: `=HYPERLINK(...)` escaping, each of `= + - @ tab CR` prefixes, plain negative numbers (`1,-2,-3.5` and `-5`), string `'-5'` escaped vs number `-5` plain, unchanged comma/quote/newline quoting, and quote-doubling inside an escaped formula.

